# vendor/inshellisense keeps its OWN git repo (with an `upstream` remote) so our
# patches stay a rebasable commit series. Don't nest it in this repo.
#
# NOTE: this is exactly why patches/ IS committed. It is regenerated output, and
# the [PATCH n/m] counter rewrites every file whenever one is added — but it is
# also the ONLY copy of our vendor changes that a fresh clone gets, so leaving it
# out made the repo unable to bootstrap itself. Churn is the lesser problem.
vendor/

# compiled spec output
specs/build/

# generated drift drafts — promote into specs/src/ after review, don't commit raw
specs/refresh/drafts/

# local frecency history (machine-specific runtime data)
frecency/*.jsonl

node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store

Agents.md
